    "license": "MIT",
    "notes": [
      "Research approximation of the 2++ color / ISO 100 / distant-subject condition; not a measured replica or an endorsed product.",
      "All optical, matrix and electron-domain values are engineering hypotheses, not measured Harinezumi hardware specifications.",
      "Use restrained optical defects, dense primary colors, soft fine detail and a short highlight shoulder. No synthetic light leaks or film grain.",
      "ISO 100 describes the research target only. Host Camera2 autoexposure and autofocus remain active, and EXIF records actual host exposure.",
      "Android uses 4:3 framing with a 3.2 megapixel output ceiling as a research delivery policy, not a verified sensor specification.",
      "Preview/still sampling, automatic white balance dynamics, focus-distance response and JPEG artifacts are not calibrated in v0.1.0.",
      "v0.2: PSF/ISP footprints and noise power scale from a 1920x1440 parameter reference. Approximation of reduced sensor area, not a fixed CFA simulation or measured sensor specification.",
      "v0.3 visual review: retain saturated object gradients rather than hard primary plateaus; open the shadow toe and reduce fixed magenta bias. References: 2010 pict0009/pict0003/pict0002 and 2025 PICT0015/PICT0017/PICT0021 on hendigi.com. Parameters are subjective hypotheses, not a fit to paired scene data.",
      "2026-09-30: visually reviewed nine owner samples from digital-harinezumi-again. Retain object texture by reducing Gaussian denoise and using restrained detail recovery. No paired scene fit; these are design hypotheses.",
      "Keep v0.3 WB, CCM and tone: saturated red surfaces still show gradients; warm buildings and cyan-blue sky coexist. Avoid a global cyan cast."
    ]
  },
